{"person_name": "Jord Parma", "traits": [{"trait_name": "openness", "score": 0.7, "confidence": 0.8, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "I am a Priest of the Spirit educated into all the mysteries, who have come here where the inner voice called me.", "start": 451, "end": 533}, {"text": "Jord Parma knew his priestly lingo well and did his job magnificently.", "start": 3663, "end": 3718}]}, {"trait_name": "extraversion", "score": 0.6, "confidence": 0.7, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "His arms went out in an embracing gesture. \"My son – my children. May you always be in the protecting arms of the Galactic Spirit.\"", "start": 222, "end": 320}, {"text": "The missionary's voice poured out as he struggled in the two-fold grasp, \"Cursed be the traitor who abandons his fellowman to evil and to death.\"", "start": 1580, "end": 1700}]}, {"trait_name": "neuroticism", "score": 0.7, "confidence": 0.8, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "The missionary started to sudden feverish life. His arms went out in an embracing gesture.", "start": 200, "end": 260}, {"text": "The sound made his eyes wild. \"You hear them? Why do you talk of law to me, of a law made by men? There are higher laws.", "start": 1000, "end": 1100}]}], "source_passage_ids": ["foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_192", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_194", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_195", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_238", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_239", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_240", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_241"]}
{"person_name": "She", "traits": [{"trait_name": "openness", "score": 0.8, "confidence": 0.9, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "I had read Gibbon's Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire not once, but twice.", "start": 122, "end": 186}, {"text": "In the 1960s and 1970s, in fact, I wrote two science-fiction novels and a mystery novel, to say nothing of well over a hundred short stories", "start": 3663, "end": 3775}]}, {"trait_name": "conscientiousness", "score": 0.7, "confidence": 0.9, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "Through the remainder of the decade, John Campbell kept my nose to the grindstone and made sure he got additional Foundation stories.", "start": 1010, "end": 1110}, {"text": "I had spent eight years on the Foundation, written nine stories with a total of about 220,000 words.", "start": 1600, "end": 1670}]}, {"trait_name": "agreeableness", "score": 0.6, "confidence": 0.7, "evidence_spans": [{"text": "Well, Campbell was the kind of editor who could not be denied, so I wrote one more Foundation story, vowing to myself that it would be the last.", "start": 1440, "end": 1530}, {"text": "He was constantly telling me I ought to finish the series and was just as constantly suggesting plot devices.", "start": 3960, "end": 4030}]}], "source_passage_ids": ["foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_1", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_2", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_3", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_4", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_5", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_6", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_7", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_8", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_10", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_11", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_13", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_22", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_23", "foundation-1-asimov-isaac-foundation-libgen-li_28"